MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and Cat Stevens feel like natural next choices because they combine melodic songs with the artist-focused greatest-hits format I have repeatedly chosen.",
    "Carole King fits the warm vocals and thoughtful songwriting I enjoy in Melanie and Simon & Garfunkel, even though Tapestry is not a hits collection."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Roger Miller's greatest-hits format fits on the surface, but country novelty songs do not match the gentler folk-pop and melodic rock I want now.",
    "Adele connects to my occasional newer-pop listening, but older songs appeal more today. Red gives me too little information to judge whether it fits."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits label alone does not make something appealing; the singing style and songs matter more.",
    "My classic-rock listening does not mean I want every kind of rock right now. Queen, the Rolling Stones and Journey have some appeal, but I am choosing gentler music today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Melanie and Simon & Garfunkel points toward warm voices, acoustic sounds and melodic songwriting, which makes Carole King and Cat Stevens especially appealing.",
    "I often choose collections centered on one artist. That makes Eagles more compelling today than a mixed soundtrack, even when its older pop and rock songs fit my taste."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older hits, but only some capture the warm, gentler sound and artist-focused listening I want today."
}
